From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:30:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 379/405] Design check: faster - the overlaps in C++ threads,
 boxes that only touch skipped, fingerprints once

A room of 125 parts: 12.9 s (18.7 with floating parts) to 10.2 s the
first time, 2.8 s again or after moving a part.
- The pairs not measured before go at once to Part.findInterferences
  (threads, the GIL let go: a Python thread keeps the screen alive),
  shapes cut into their solids; a pair that fails there is measured
  again solid by solid, and said if it still cannot be.
- findInterferences leaves out boxes that share no more than minVolume:
  the overlap is inside both boxes (parts on the floor only touch).
- The pair cache's fingerprint is taken once per shape, without volume
  and area; isValid is remembered by fingerprint.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
